      "lineNbr": 280,
      "author": {
        "id": 1523797
      },
      "writtenOn": "2025-09-30T19:16:26Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "The datasheet requires that the regulator be disabled (EN pin low) while adjusting these parameters. That\u0027s what the board-specific implementations do in the following CL. However:\n\n(1) We are trying to discourage further usage of strong/weak board override functions and a callback-based mechanism where the board can register a hook for before and after the PMIC update would be better\n\n(2) Since the PMIC requires being disabled, it might be worthwhile to have the driver do this directly and have a particular GPIO referenced in its devicetree node that controls `EN`, but this one is also a power sequencing signal and the AP needs to be turned down, so it isn\u0027t as straightforward.",
      "parentUuid": "3b05ee28_a67283fe",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 280,
        "startChar": 19,
        "endLine": 280,
        "endChar": 53
      },
      "revId": "d098d4061a40d7046d6594423cb0cd3f1520cc28",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba"
